  "rules": [
    "When recent history shows a strong downtrend (e.g., Example 1) and sentiment is neutral or slightly positive, the model systematically overestimates future prices by ignoring immediate mean reversion; apply a downward correction of 5-8% to the forecasted path.",
    "When history exhibits high volatility with a recent spike followed by mixed sentiment (positive/negative), the model fails to capture the 'spike-and-fall' pattern, resulting in an upward bias; reduce the forecasted trajectory by approximately 4-6 EUR per month.",
    "In volatile regimes where sentiment shifts from positive to negative within the last 5 days, the model's linear extrapolation creates a significant overshoot; apply a mean-reversion correction that pulls the forecast closer to the historical average of the preceding 10 days.",
    "The model consistently underestimates short-term volatility and over-smooths price action during high-sentiment periods; increase the variance of the forecast distribution or apply a jaggedness adjustment factor of +2% to daily steps."
  ]
}
